IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpfta-unfair-practices`

-- Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003 (Singapore), Part 3 -- additional consumer rights in respect of non-conforming goods
-- (the "lemon law"): when Part 3 applies and the 6-month presumption (s 14, with s 13(3)), repair or replacement (s 15), reduction
-- or rescission (s 16), waiting before rejecting the goods (s 17), and the reduction of a refund for use (ss 16(3), 18(5)).
--
-- SEAT: the consumer who bought, acquired or hired the goods -- in Part 3's words the "transferee" (the buyer, the transferee under
-- the Supply of Goods Act 1982, or the hirer). The "transferor" is called the seller here.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 9 March 2025 (SSO "Current version as at 30 Sep 2026"),
-- as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CPFTA2003.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: whether the goods conform to the contract (s 13(4) points into the Sale of Goods Act 1979, the Supply of Goods Act 1982
-- and the Hire-Purchase Act 1969, none deposited: asked as a fact); "deals as consumer" (s 13(2) borrows Part 1 of the Unfair Contract
-- Terms Act 1977: asked as a fact, with s 13(3)'s burden on the seller); the court's powers to switch remedies and set terms (s 18(2)
-- to (4), (6), (7)); the amount of an "appropriate" reduction. Section 15(2)'s duty to repair "within a reasonable time" has no
-- stated period, so it is not written as a regulative rule with a deadline.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual to
-- whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass,
-- no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003 -- Part 3, non-conforming goods`

§§ `13(3), 14 -- does Part 3 give me rights over these goods`

-- s 14(1): "This Part applies if -- (a) the transferee deals as consumer; (b) the goods do not conform to the applicable contract at
-- the time of delivery; and (c) the contract was made on or after 1 September 2012." s 13(1): an "applicable contract" is a contract
-- of sale of goods, a contract for the transfer of goods, or a hire-purchase agreement. s 13(3): "it is for a transferor claiming
-- that the transferee does not deal as consumer to show that the transferee does not."
-- s 14(3): goods "which do not conform to the applicable contract at any time within the period of 6 months starting after the date
-- on which the goods were delivered ... must be taken not to have so conformed at that date." (4): not "if -- (a) it is established
-- that the goods did so conform at that date; or (b) its application is incompatible with the nature of the goods or the nature of
-- the lack of conformity."
-- The 6 months are counted to the same day 6 months on (a day that month lacks falls back to its last day); a lack of conformity on
-- the day of delivery itself is s 14(1)(b) directly. Both are inferences from "starting after"; the text gives no rule for the count.
DECLARE `My goods` HAS
    `the seller has shown that I did not deal as consumer`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a sale or transfer of goods or a hire-purchase agreement`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the contract was made`                                         IS A DATE
    `the date the goods were delivered`                                      IS A DATE
    `the goods are shown not to have conformed at delivery`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date a lack of conformity was found`                                IS A MAYBE DATE
    `it is established that the goods conformed at delivery`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court finds the 6-month rule incompatible with the goods or the defect` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN goods IS A `My goods`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my goods taken not to have conformed at delivery` IF
        goods's `the goods are shown not to have conformed at delivery`
    OR  (    `found within 6 months of delivery`
         AND NOT goods's `it is established that the goods conformed at delivery`
         AND NOT goods's `the court finds the 6-month rule incompatible with the goods or the defect`)
  WHERE
    `found within 6 months of delivery` MEANS
        CONSIDER goods's `the date a lack of conformity was found`
        WHEN JUST f THEN     DATE_SERIAL f AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL (goods's `the date the goods were delivered`)
                         AND DATE_SERIAL f AT MOST DATE_SERIAL (`months after` (goods's `the date the goods were delivered`) 6)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN goods IS A `My goods`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does Part 3 give me rights over these goods` IF
        NOT goods's `the seller has shown that I did not deal as consumer`
    AND goods's `it is a sale or transfer of goods or a hire-purchase agreement`
    AND `Are my goods taken not to have conformed at delivery` goods
    AND DATE_SERIAL (goods's `the date the contract was made`) AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2012)

§§ `15 -- repair or replacement`

-- (1): "If section 14 applies, the transferee may require the transferor to -- (a) repair the goods; or (b) replace the goods."
-- (3): "The transferee must not require the transferor to repair or (as the case may be) replace the goods if that remedy is -- (a)
-- impossible; (b) disproportionate in comparison to the other of those remedies; or (c) disproportionate in comparison to an
-- appropriate reduction ... or rescission". (4): disproportionate means it "imposes costs on the transferor which, in comparison to
-- those imposed ... by the other, are unreasonable", weighing the value of conforming goods, the significance of the lack of
-- conformity, and whether the other remedy avoids significant inconvenience. Disproportion is a judgment for the court: each is an
-- input, read "if the court finds ...".
-- (2): once required, the transferor "must -- (a) repair or ... replace the goods within a reasonable time and without causing
-- significant inconvenience to the transferee; and (b) bear any necessary costs incurred in doing so (including in particular the cost
-- of any labour, materials or postage)."
DECLARE `The remedies` HAS
    `repair is impossible`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `replacement is impossible`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `repair is disproportionate to replacement`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `replacement is disproportionate to repair`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `repair is disproportionate to a reduction or rescission`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `replacement is disproportionate to a reduction or rescission`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have required repair or replacement`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the seller failed to do it in a reasonable time without significant inconvenience to me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the seller has had a reasonable time to do it`                          IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN goods IS A `My goods`, r IS A `The remedies`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I require the seller to repair the goods` IF
        `Does Part 3 give me rights over these goods` goods
    AND NOT r's `repair is impossible`
    AND NOT r's `repair is disproportionate to replacement`
    AND NOT r's `repair is disproportionate to a reduction or rescission`

GIVEN goods IS A `My goods`, r IS A `The remedies`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I require the seller to replace the goods` IF
        `Does Part 3 give me rights over these goods` goods
    AND NOT r's `replacement is impossible`
    AND NOT r's `replacement is disproportionate to repair`
    AND NOT r's `replacement is disproportionate to a reduction or rescission`

GIVEN goods IS A `My goods`, r IS A `The remedies`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the seller bear the cost of the repair or replacement` IF
        `Does Part 3 give me rights over these goods` goods
    AND r's `I have required repair or replacement`

§§ `16 -- reduction in price or rescission`

-- (1): "If section 14 applies, the transferee may -- (a) require the transferor to reduce the amount to be paid ... by an appropriate
-- amount; or (b) rescind the contract with regard to those goods, if the condition in subsection (2) is satisfied." (2): "(a) by
-- virtue of section 15(3) the transferee may require neither repair nor replacement of the goods; or (b) the transferee has required
-- the transferor to repair or replace the goods, but the transferor is in breach of the requirement of section 15(2)(a)".
-- So a consumer cannot go straight to a refund where repair or replacement is still open: repair or replacement comes first.
GIVEN goods IS A `My goods`, r IS A `The remedies`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask for a price reduction or rescind the contract` IF
        `Does Part 3 give me rights over these goods` goods
    AND (    (    NOT `May I require the seller to repair the goods` goods r
              AND NOT `May I require the seller to replace the goods` goods r)
         OR  (    r's `I have required repair or replacement`
              AND r's `the seller failed to do it in a reasonable time without significant inconvenience to me`))

-- s 16(3): "if the transferee rescinds the contract, any reimbursement to the transferee may be reduced to take account of the use the
-- transferee has had of the goods since they were delivered"; s 18(5) gives the court the same power. It is a "may": the answer is
-- whether the reduction is open, not whether it will be made.
GIVEN `I have rescinded the contract` IS A BOOLEAN, `I have used the goods since delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my refund be reduced for my use of the goods` IF
        `I have rescinded the contract`
    AND `I have used the goods since delivery`

§§ `17 -- waiting before I reject the goods`

-- (1): "If the transferee requires the transferor to repair or replace the goods, the transferee must not act under subsection (2)
-- until the transferee has given the transferor a reasonable time in which to repair or replace". (2): the transferee acts under it
-- if "(a) the transferee rejects the goods and terminates the contract for breach of condition; or (b) the transferee requires the
-- goods to be repaired or replaced, as the case may be". Read literally (b) is the very requirement (1) presupposes; it is read here
-- as a further demand of repair or replacement (an inference). The question answered is only whether s 17 holds the consumer back;
-- whether the right to reject exists is for the Sale of Goods Act 1979, not deposited.
GIVEN r IS A `The remedies`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I wait before rejecting the goods or demanding another remedy` IF
        r's `I have required repair or replacement`
    AND NOT r's `the seller has had a reasonable time to do it`
